TODO items for mcstas-ess-instr-citool
======================================

* runci: Consider running the tests of the different modes in parallel (as
  independent mctest runs, each with its own test directory), to make CI
  faster for projects with several modes. MPI (runci --mpi) does not help
  much for typical tests, since compilation with MPI takes longer, and the
  default mctest simulations are short.

* runci: The JSON test results produced by mctest are only used to check for
  failures which mctest did not report in its exit code (see check_results
  in runtest.py). Decide whether to use them for anything else (e.g.
  summarise, store as CI artifacts, compare between runs).

* generatepy: The test code generated by mcstas-pygen sets and restores the
  instrument parameters around add_test calls. With McStasScript 0.0.94 (now
  required), add_test(..., parameters={...}) could be used instead, in
  mcstas-pygen and in the ExPyHelpers and ExPyExtra examples.

* Top-level files: CONTRIBUTING* is allowed (like README*, TODO*, LICENSE*
  and CHANGELOG*), since the ESS instrument template had a CONTRIBUTING.md
  with the contacts of the project (IDS, instrument team, McStas
  developers). Decide whether such files should be required in general,
  e.g. a CONTRIBUTING.md with the contacts, or a LICENSE (the template's is
  still a placeholder).

* localdata/: Consider a size limit (or a policy for large files, e.g. Git
  LFS) for data files. In the surveyed instrument repositories, the largest
  data file is a 38 MB .hkl file (MAGiC).

* McStasScript: instr.add_search(cmd, SHELL=True) writes a "SEARCH SHELL"
  statement, but also tries to load components from a folder named like the
  command itself (printing "Did not find specified folder"), so components
  found only via the command cannot be used with add_component. Propose a
  McStasScript PR which runs the command (as McStas does) and loads the
  components from the resulting directories. This is needed for the
  translation of SEARCH SHELL statements by mcstas-pygen (see next item).
  Any file lookup added in that PR must follow the locations searched by
  McStas's Open_File() (read_table-lib), which will no longer include $HOME
  (see the NCrystal search path item below). McStasScript itself does not
  currently search $HOME.

* generatepy: Since McStas 3.9.0
  (https://github.com/mccode-dev/McCode/pull/2718), mcstas-pygen translates
  SEARCH statements into instr.add_search() calls, but only relative to the
  generated script if the script is written into the working directory (the
  instr/ directory). Otherwise, as in generatepy, which writes it to a
  temporary directory, the paths are absolute paths of the source project.
  Also, the generated make() uses the directory of the script (i.e. the
  python package) as default input_path. generatepy therefore removes both,
  and adds its own code for localcomps/ and localdata/. Consider whether
  mcstas-pygen should get an option to write paths relative to the final
  location of the script.

* NCrystal custom search directories (ncrystal_add_custom_search_dir, used
  by mccode_setup_ncrystal_search_paths in McCode):
  - Bug: NCrystal::DataSources::addCustomSearchDirectory asserts strictly
    decreasing priorities after sorting, but the C API always uses the same
    default priority, so adding two different directories violates the
    assertion (harmless in normal builds, where it is compiled out).
  - Custom directories have a lower priority than NCrystal's standard library,
    so a local file with the same name as a standard library file (e.g.
    Al_sg225.ncmat next to the .instr file) is shadowed by the standard
    library version (unless it is in the working directory), unlike McStas's
    Open_File(). Also, paths containing ".." are not accepted in custom
    directories.
  Perhaps an NCrystal JSON query could allow more flexible modifications,
  including of priorities. To be determined later; the McCode side
  (mccode_setup_ncrystal_search_paths) can then be updated accordingly.

* Components which read data files by fixed file names do not find them in
  localdata/ (McStas looks in the working directory, next to the .instr file
  and in the McStas data directories). For Union_abs_logger_nD_scintillator
  (used by SKADI), the parameter table_dir was added for this
  (https://github.com/mccode-dev/McCode/pull/2720, in McStas 3.9.0). Other
  components might need similar parameters.

* Instrument repositories at git.esss.dk/dmsc-instrumentmodels: TBL and SKADI
  use the standard layout, and standard-layout branches exist for FREIA,
  ODIN, HEIMDAL, NMX, BEER, LOKI, ESTIA, MAGiC and the ESS instrument
  template (T-REX is not converted). All of them require McStas 3.9.0 and
  pass runci with it (5 October 2026).
